.SS "void csmp::dN_To2DOF (uint32_t nodes, \fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & B)"

.PP
FEM matrix transformations, for the case where the solution variable is a vector in 2D, Zienkewicz, volume 1, p\&. 22\&. Converts (global) interpolation function derivative matrix into form where it can be multiplied, for instance, with a 2DOF material property matrix or for computation of 2D stiffness matrix\&. 
.br

.PP
Original B: 
.PP
.nf
| dN0dx dN1dx \&.\&.\&. dN(nodes)dx |

.fi
.PP
 B = | dN0dy dN1dy \&.\&.\&. dN(nodes)dy |

.PP
Transformed B (see Zienkiewicz Vol\&.1 p\&. 48, eq\&. 3\&.10b): 
.PP
.nf
| dN0dx   0   dN1dx  \&.\&.\&. dN(nodes)dx   0   |

.fi
.PP
 B = | 0 dN0dy 0 \&.\&.\&. 0 dN(nodes)dy | | dN0dy dN0dx dN1dy \&.\&.\&. dN5dy dN(nodes)dx |
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The shape function derivative matrix DN for 1 degree of freedom per node\&.

.PP
The expanded matrix is returned into the input matrix\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To pre-process DN matrices in multi-DOF computations\&. 
.br
 
.PP
.nf
@test OK SKM refactored and retested 2/12/2014

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "void csmp::dN_To3DOF (uint32_t nodes, \fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & B)"

.PP
FEM matrix transformations, for the case where the solution variable is a vector in 3D, Zienkewicz, volume 1, p\&. 133\&. Transformation of interpolation function derivative matrix to 3 vectorial degrees of freedom per node as shown in Zienkewicz, vol\&. 1, p\&.133\&.

.PP
\fBTest\fP
.RS 4
OK SKM retested 2/12/2014 
.RE
.PP

