.SS "void csmp::normalAndShearStressOnPlane (const \fBTensorVariable\fP< 3U > & ts, const \fBPoint\fP< 3U > & un, double & sigma_n, double & sigma_s)"

.PP
uses Cauchy's formula to resolve normal and magnitude of shear stress on a surface defined by its normal Solves for the surface normal and tangential stresses, i\&.e\&. the first and second term in the equation, 
.br

.PP
t = (t \&. n) n + n x (t x n) 
.br

.PP
respectively, using Cauchy's formula\&. For description see Pollard & Fletcher, p\&. 215\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument is a tensor of the Cartesian stresses (as opposed to the principal stresses)\&. The second argument is the outward-pointing unit normal to the surface of interest\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The computed stress components are returned into the 3rd and 4th function arguments\&. 
.RE
.PP

